WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.030 align:start position:0%
 
ladies and gentlemen  dear participants the ocean race has now  been sailing the waves for almost  50 years the ocean is your arena  and every day you feel its unique  strength  and power but you also  sense and see its growing fragility  you've seen it change and suffer  and you are helping it to heal  you have been removing plastics from the  ocean  you have been tackling pollution with  your own hands  you have been raising awareness on ocean  rights  and campaigning for action on  overfishing  i very much welcome the fact that this  summer several teams will carry  scientific equipment on board  this will help measure microplastics in  the water  and collect data about the impact of  climate change on the seas  although the ocean can produce a mighty  roar  as its waves crash on our shores  it has no voice in our public debates  so i salute you for speaking up for it  at events like today's summit  like you the european commission wants  to see a notion  that is healthy and full of life  biodiversity loss is one of the greatest  threats  to our planet and to human health  our seas and oceans are a particular  concern  they are our most natural ally in the  fight against climate change  and they are the first to feel its  effects  and that is why last month the  commission set out a new approach for  sustainable  blue economy in the european union  because in addition to having a crucial  role in regulating our climate  the ocean's rich biodiversity  provides us with essential goods and  services  it is critical for energy production for  tourism  for transport or trade the blue economy  provides  4.5 million jobs in the european union  alone  but for sustainable future  all blue economy sectors will have to  reduce their environmental  and climate impact because  tackling the climate and biodiversity  crisis  requires healthy seeds and we have to  make sustainable use of their resources  and this is why we are also promoting  across the world  the eu's expertise environmental action  and innovative business solutions  to support this i can announce that we  will update our  international ocean agenda next year  the commission will lead efforts on a  global agreement on plastics  and it will embed a circular approach  across our economy ahead of this year's  crucial biodiversity crop 15 in china  and the climate cop 26 in the uk we will  also  focus our diplomatic energy on  protecting  our oceans for example  the eu and its member states are  proposing to establish  two new large-scale marine protected  areas in the southern ocean we will do  this together with a number of  like-minded partners  if approved they would protect an area  of over  3 million square kilometers  and as we head to kunming in october for  the biodiversity cup 15  we are working towards global  commitments  our aim is to protect 30 percent of our  land and sea  a commitment we have already made at  european level  and now we are also working to increase  global climate ambition  at cup 26 in glasgow europe has already  committed to reach climate neutrality by  2050  it is our historic duty to reduce  emissions  and pollution to bring us back into  balance with the limits of  our planet in glasgow  and in kunming we want to see even  more international partners joining us  ladies and gentlemen as you race with  purpose  across our ocean we too race with  purpose towards net zero let us sail  together  and let's hope for fair winds thank you

